+- [ ] **PREVIEW-009**: When admitting a completed preview would exceed the cache budget, the preview worker SHALL evict the least recently used entry from the first-use queue (the queue of sheets requested once) and record its key in the ghost list (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets) before evicting any entry from the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-010**: When admitting or promoting a sheet into the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once) would exceed the hot queue's configured cap, the preview worker SHALL evict hot-queue entries by least recent use until the sheet fits within the cap, and SHALL NOT evict entries from the first-use queue (the queue of sheets requested once) to satisfy that cap.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-011**: While a sheet is larger than the hot queue's (the queue of sheets requested more than once) configured cap, the preview worker SHALL NOT admit that sheet to the hot queue.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-012**: When the bytes held by the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once) grow and the two queues together would exceed the cache budget, the preview worker SHALL evict first-use-queue (the queue of sheets requested once) entries by least recent use and record each evicted key in the ghost list (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets), before evicting any entry from the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-013**: While cached previews are held, the preview worker SHALL keep the total bytes of JPEG data resident in the first-use queue (the queue of sheets requested once) and the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once) within the 12 GiB cache budget at every instant, including while concurrent render jobs complete.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-014**: When a rendered sheet is larger than the cache budget, the preview worker SHALL serve the sheet to the requester without caching it.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-015**: When a preview key held in the ghost list (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets) is rendered again and the rendered sheet is no larger than the cache budget, the preview worker SHALL restore the ghost entry's reference count to the key before that request's reference count is incremented, SHALL admit the sheet to the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once), or to the first-use queue (the queue of sheets requested once) if the sheet is larger than the hot queue's configured cap, and SHALL remove the key from the ghost list.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-016**: When the ghost list (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets) holds its configured maximum number of keys and a new key must be recorded, the preview worker SHALL drop the oldest ghost entry.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-017**: While cached previews are held, the preview worker SHALL NOT count ghost-list keys (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets) toward the cache budget for cached preview bytes.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-018**: When the worker starts, the preview worker SHALL admit cached files present on disk to the first-use queue (the queue of sheets requested once) with no reference history and SHALL start with an empty ghost list (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets).
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-019**: While a preview sheet is being served, the preview worker SHALL NOT evict that sheet.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-020**: While four rendering jobs are active, the preview worker SHALL NOT start another render job.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-021**: When a request misses the cache and no render job is already pending for that preview key, the preview worker SHALL return 202 with a job ticket and a two-second retry interval.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-022**: When a render job completes or fails, the preview worker SHALL remove the job's temporary render output.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-023**: When the preview worker evicts a cached preview, the preview worker SHALL NOT delete source footage and SHALL NOT change the semantics of any outstanding job ticket.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-024**: While render jobs are waiting for an active slot, the preview worker SHALL start them in the order they were enqueued.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-025**: When a request is served from the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once), the preview worker SHALL mark that sheet as the hot queue's most recently used entry.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-026**: When a sheet is evicted from the first-use queue (the queue of sheets requested once), the preview worker SHALL record the evicted key and its reference count in the ghost list (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets), and SHALL NOT record a key that is already present in the ghost list; when a sheet is evicted from the hot queue (the queue of sheets requested more than once), the preview worker SHALL discard that key's reference count.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-027**: When the preview worker caches a rendered preview, the preview worker SHALL key it by clip ID, revision, and renderer version.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-028**: When a rendered sheet is larger than the cache budget, the preview worker SHALL retain any ghost-list entry (the list of keys of evicted first-use sheets) for its key.
+- [ ] **PREVIEW-029**: The preview worker SHALL NOT count temporary render output toward the cache budget.
